          "type": "header",
          "bbox": [
            0.681,
            0.071,
            0.813,
            0.089
          ],
          "content": "Quadrilaterals"
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.852,
            0.071,
            0.881,
            0.087
          ],
          "content": "57"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.192,
            0.109,
            0.881,
            0.151
          ],
          "content": "(a) If a quadrilateral is a parallelogram, then its opposite sides are equal."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.236,
            0.156,
            0.88,
            0.208
          ],
          "content": "**Converse:** If the opposite sides of a quadrilateral are equal, then it is a parallelogram. Is this converse statement true? Is this converse statement true?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.191,
            0.222,
            0.881,
            0.264
          ],
          "content": "(b) If a quadrilateral is a parallelogram, then the opposite angles are equal."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.236,
            0.269,
            0.88,
            0.33
          ],
          "content": "**Converse:** If the opposite angles of a quadrilateral are equal, then it is a parallelogram. Is this converse statement true?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.193,
            0.335,
            0.881,
            0.377
          ],
          "content": "(c) If a quadrilateral is a parallelogram, then its diagonals bisect each other."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.236,
            0.381,
            0.881,
            0.443
          ],
          "content": "**Converse:** If the diagonals of a quadrilateral bisect each other, then it is a parallelogram. Is this converse statement true?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.153,
            0.449,
            0.736,
            0.469
          ],
          "content": "Can you experiment and guess what the answers are?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.474,
            0.881,
            0.514
          ],
          "content": "It turns out that all three converse statements are true. To demonstrate this, it is useful to recall how we had proved Theorem 1:"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.153,
            0.518,
            0.388,
            0.537
          ],
          "content": "**Proof of Theorem 1:**"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.544,
            0.32,
            0.664
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [
            {
              "bbox": [
                0.191,
                0.675,
                0.223,
                0.693
              ],
              "content": "(a)"
            }
          ],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_6_image_11.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.319,
            0.548,
            0.594,
            0.666
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [
            {
              "bbox": [
                0.425,
                0.674,
                0.456,
                0.693
              ],
              "content": "(b)"
            }
          ],
          "footnotes": [],
